## 5. Jenkins Docker Credentials

Go to:

Manage Jenkins → Credentials → Global credentials → Add Credentials

Configure:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Kind | Username with password |
| Username | Docker Hub username |
| Password | Docker Hub Personal Access Token |
| ID | dockerhub-credentials |

In the Freestyle job:

1. Open Configure.
2. Go to Build Environment.
3. Enable Use secret text(s) or file(s).
4. Add Username and password (separated).

Set:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Username Variable | DOCKER_USER |
| Password Variable | DOCKER_PASS |
| Credentials | dockerhub-credentials |

Do not put your Docker Hub password or token directly in the shell script.

