## 11. Maven Permission Troubleshooting

Previously, Maven showed:

```text
Failed to delete webapp/target/webapp.war
```

Another error was:

```text
maven-surefire-plugin:2.11:test

Error creating properties files for forking

java.io.IOException: Permission denied
```

The WAR file was owned by `root`, which can cause permission problems for Jenkins.

If you have SSH access to EC2, run:

```bash
sudo chown -R jenkins:jenkins \
  /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/Maven

sudo chmod -R u+rwX \
  /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/Maven
```

Then change Maven Goals back to:

`clean install`

Save the job and run Build Now.

If the error continues, inspect the workspace ownership and Maven Surefire temporary-file location.

Do not change permissions outside the Jenkins workspace without checking ownership.

